# Studio environment variable NAMES only — never values.
#
# Sanity requires the `SANITY_STUDIO_` prefix for any variable bundled into the Studio, which is
# a useful reminder of what these are: they end up in a client-side build and are therefore
# PUBLIC IDENTIFIERS, not secrets.
#
# The Studio never carries a token. It authenticates the editor through Sanity's own login.
# TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md §18's three tokens all live elsewhere:
#   - read-only Viewer token  → the web build environment (see ../.env.example)
#   - draft/preview token     → the preview deployment only, server-side
#   - Editor/write token      → nowhere in this system

SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=
SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=

# Optional. Set only once the access-controlled preview deployment exists (§6.2), to enable the
# Presentation tool. Leave empty until then.
# SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_URL=
